course: dictionary
lesson: 9455
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Starch is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «Starchy foods» are the first meaning: foods like bread, rice and potatoes, which give the body energy.
explain: «Bread goes stale as its starch slowly lines up and squeezes out water.» Starch here is part of the food, not a spray. The clue is bread, which is food. Ask yourself what would fit: a part of food, or a powder for clothes?
explain: The verb starch means to make cloth stiff. In history, «collars and shirts were starched stiff», so the clue is cloth and shirts. This is the clothes meaning.
fact: Starch is a white substance found in foods such as bread, rice, pasta and potatoes.
fact: Starch gives the body energy, so starchy foods are energy foods.
fact: As a noun, starch can also be a powder or spray used to make clothes stiff.
fact: As a verb, starch means to make cloth stiff with starch. Its forms are starches, starched and starching.
fact: In a science test, iodine solution turns blue-black when there is starch in a food.
exercise: «Bread goes stale as its starch slowly lines up and squeezes out water.» In this sentence, starch means | *A substance in food | A spray for shirts | A kind of cloth | A powder for clothes
exercise: Nadia says starch only means something for clothes. What is the fuller answer? | Starch is only a spray for shirts | *Starch is in foods like bread and rice, and it is also a powder for clothes | Starch is a colour | Starch is a kind of cloth
exercise: «Collars and shirts were starched stiff.» What does starched mean here? | *Made stiff with starch | Torn into pieces | Dyed bright red | Washed in warm water
test: Which of these is a starchy food? | Chalk | Water | *Potatoes | Cardboard
test: In the iodine test, what colour does a food turn if it has starch? | Yellow | Red | *Blue-black | Green
exam: «Plants make starch in their leaves from sugar to store energy.» In this sentence, starch means | *A substance that stores energy | A powder for clothes | To make cloth stiff | A kind of bread
